# Storage and file browser (bootloader)

Spec: `docs/core/05-storage-and-paths.md` (tree, config keys, `app/storage.py`) and `docs/modules/file-browser.md` (API, registry, UI). Decision: ADR-005.

## Invariants
- Two roots: `SOURCE_PATH` (question library, read-mostly) and `STORAGE_PATH` = `Shared/<SUBJECT>` (admin rw / user ro / viewer hidden, `_archive` super-admin) + `System/` (caches, staging) + `User/<username>/` (`generated/` is read-only in the browser; owned by My Files).
- **Every join goes through `storage.safe_join(base, *rel)`**; `None` = outside the root = 403/404. Never `startswith`. Storage must be on the same drive as Source (drive gate).
- Paths come from `storage.source_path()/shared_path()/system_path()/user_path()/...` (which read `current_app.config`), never `os.getenv`.
- Username = folder name: validated by `utils.validate_username` (`^[A-Za-z0-9._-]{1,80}$`, no leading/trailing dot, reserved names); renaming a user moves `User/<old>` → `User/<new>`. `storage.safe_username` sanitises legacy names.
- `RootRegistry(user, scope)`: **user scope** (default; also for super admins) = personal `user` root + `shared:<SID>` per subject; **admin scope** (`Source`, `Storage`, `FILE_BROWSER_EXTRA_ROOTS`) only for super admins — a non-super request for `scope=admin` is silently downgraded. `/admin/files` is the only admin-scope client.
- All mutating ops check `Root.can_write`; read-only roots reject upload/rename/delete/mkdir/copy/move. `/files/api/move` refuses moving into or out of `generated/`.
- Uploads: every path component through `secure_filename`; folder uploads preserve structure via `paths[]` but stay inside the target.
- `FILE_BROWSER_EXTRA_ROOTS` is a JSON list row in `system_settings`, deliberately outside the settings REGISTRY; managed by the roots routes only.
- Backends that accept a location take `{root, rel_path}` and resolve through the user's registry (PDF Import `_resolve_server_pdf`, Toolbox `_resolve_root_base(root_id, require_write)`).

## Frontend
- Both browser pages share `partials/file_browser_{css,body,js}.html`; the picker is `partials/file_selector.html` → `OQBFileSelector.open({mode:'file'|'folder', extensions, multiple, preferRootId, locationKey, onPick})` returning `{root_id, root_label, rel_path, name, token}`; always user scope. Pass `fb_scope='admin'` + `fb_can_manage_roots=True` only on `admin_files.html`.

## Gotchas
- Sibling-prefix trap (`Q:\Source` vs `Q:\SourceBackup`) is exactly why `safe_join` exists.
- `ensure_storage_tree()` is best-effort at boot; missing dirs are not an error path you should "fix" with chmod-style hacks.
- `cli.py migrate-storage` is idempotent and dry-run by default; never pass `--no-dry-run` unasked.
